{
 "id": "styletest",
 "fps": 30,
 "lead": 1.6,
 "total": 67.752,
 "cues": [
  {
   "key": "c01",
   "beat": "b1",
   "text": "Two armies face each other at dawn.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 1.6,
   "dur": 1.942
  },
  {
   "key": "c02",
   "beat": "b1",
   "text": "Between them, in a chariot, stands the finest archer of his age.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 3.762,
   "dur": 3.702
  },
  {
   "key": "c03",
   "beat": "b1",
   "text": "And his hands begin to shake.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 7.684,
   "dur": 1.18
  },
  {
   "key": "c04",
   "beat": "b2",
   "text": "His mouth goes dry.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 9.914,
   "dur": 0.958
  },
  {
   "key": "c05",
   "beat": "b2",
   "text": "His limbs give way.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 11.092,
   "dur": 1.318
  },
  {
   "key": "c06",
   "beat": "b2",
   "text": "His bow slips from his hand.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 12.63,
   "dur": 1.537
  },
  {
   "key": "c07",
   "beat": "b2",
   "text": "He sits down in the chariot, and says: I will not fight.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 14.837,
   "dur": 4.526
  },
  {
   "key": "c08",
   "beat": "b3",
   "text": "Then the man holding the reins does something strange.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 19.913,
   "dur": 2.244
  },
  {
   "key": "c09",
   "beat": "b3",
   "text": "He smiles.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 22.377,
   "dur": 0.629
  },
  {
   "key": "c10",
   "beat": "b4",
   "text": "Bhagavad Gita. Chapter two, verse ten.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 24.656,
   "dur": 2.891
  },
  {
   "key": "c11",
   "beat": "b4",
   "text": "And Krishna, as if smiling, spoke these words to him, sinking in despair between the two armies.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 30.967,
   "dur": 5.287
  },
  {
   "key": "c12",
   "beat": "b5",
   "text": "Why would anyone smile at a man who is falling apart?",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 38.004,
   "dur": 2.397
  },
  {
   "key": "c13",
   "beat": "b5",
   "text": "Start with who is holding the reins.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 40.621,
   "dur": 1.835
  },
  {
   "key": "c14",
   "beat": "b6",
   "text": "An older text, the Katha Upanishad, draws the picture.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 43.606,
   "dur": 3.13
  },
  {
   "key": "c15",
   "beat": "b6",
   "text": "Your body is the chariot.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 46.956,
   "dur": 1.337
  },
  {
   "key": "c16",
   "beat": "b6",
   "text": "The senses are the horses.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 48.513,
   "dur": 1.243
  },
  {
   "key": "c17",
   "beat": "b6",
   "text": "The mind is the reins.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 49.976,
   "dur": 1.304
  },
  {
   "key": "c18",
   "beat": "b6",
   "text": "The intellect is the driver.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 51.5,
   "dur": 1.163
  },
  {
   "key": "c19",
   "beat": "b6",
   "text": "And you, the self, are the one riding.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 52.883,
   "dur": 2.582
  },
  {
   "key": "c20",
   "beat": "b7",
   "text": "Arjuna's horses had bolted.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 56.815,
   "dur": 1.695
  },
  {
   "key": "c21",
   "beat": "b7",
   "text": "But the reins were still in steady hands.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 58.73,
   "dur": 1.555
  },
  {
   "key": "c22",
   "beat": "b8",
   "text": "What Krishna says next, the whole of chapter two, is how to take them back.",
   "voice": "minimax@1.12",
   "start": 61.435,
   "dur": 3.697
  }
 ]
}